attributes.gen_ai.tool.definitions:
[{"type":"function","name":"exec","description":"Run JavaScript in OpenClaw. Set `title` to a 3–7 word purpose. Guest work and inline tool waits share a 10000 ms wall-clock budget per `exec`/`wait`; approvals pause it. Guest computation over this budget times out; pending tools may return `waiting` for `wait`. Use the shell tool `exec` for heavier computation. Enabled tools are async global functions. Await dependent calls in order; independent calls may run with Promise.all. Declared output fields may feed later calls in the same program; avoid extra inspection calls. Emit output with `text(value)` or `json(value)`. Return the final value, otherwise `null`. Oversized final objects/arrays may return `value.reference`. `-> ?` means unknown output: do not feed it into guessed field-dependent logic in the same program. Return it raw or `await results.save(value)`; use a later `exec` for dependent composition. Save returns `{id,bytes,count,shape,preview,previewTruncated}`: emit that descriptor directly; full JSON stays stored. Load/delete this run via `results.load(id)`/`results.delete(id)`; contract: `API.read("results.d.ts")`. For omitted tools, use `catalog.search(query)`; results are callable: `const [tool] = await catalog.search("..."); return await tool({...});`. Use handle `describe()` for schemas. `setTimeout` and `clearTimeout` work. `TextEncoder`/`TextDecoder` convert local text and bytes. Console log/info/warn/error/debug emit bounded text. Nested calls enforce normal tool policy and approvals. Tool failures are catchable; inspect possible effects before retrying. Nested results are intact or throw resource errors. Cell reply inbox: 10485760 bytes; consume replies or paginate if full. Output/value/errors share 65536 bytes across waits. Other truncation reports original JSON prefixes/omitted bytes; rerun with narrower args. Output is incremental; changed cumulative summaries replace earlier ones. Node.js modules and `require`/`import` are NOT available; use tools for external actions. Read types with `API.list(prefix?)` and `API.read(path)`; native tools: `tools/`. Types are documentation; write plain JavaScript. Swarm globals `agents.run`, `phase`, and `log` are available; read `agents.d.ts` for types and orchestration idioms. Skills are available through the async `skills` global: use `await skills.list()` and `await skills.read(name)`. `code` is JavaScript, never a shell command; do not retry failed shell source.

Enabled async tool globals (descriptions are intentionally deferred):
Each line is `callableName input -> output`; `-> ?` means unknown output.
- agents_wait { ids: Array<string>; timeoutSeconds?: number /* >= 0 */ } -> { completed: Array<{ result: string; runId: string; sessionKey: string; status: "done" | "failed" | "killed" | "timeout"; error?: string; label?: string; schemaError?: string; structured?: unknown; usage?: { inputTokens: number; outputTokens: number } }>; pending: Array<string>; errors?: Array<{ error: "not_found" | "not_owner"; runId: string }>; success?: false }
- apply_patch { input: string } -> { summary: { added: Array<string>; deleted: Array<string>; modified: Array<string> } }
- conversations_list { channel?: string; limit?: number /* integer, >= 1 */; query?: string } -> { conversations: Array<{ accountId: string; channel: string; conversationRef: string; firstSeenAt: number; kind: "direct" | "group" | "channel"; lastSeenAt: number; target: string; label?: string; threadId?: string }> }
- conversations_send { conversationRef: string; message: string } -> { channel: string; conversationRef: string; status: "sent" | "queued" | "suppressed" | "unknown"; messageId?: string; queueId?: string }
- conversations_turn { conversationRef: string; message: string; timeoutSeconds?: number /* integer, >= 1, <= 300 */ } -> { channel: string; conversationRef: string; correlationPersisted: boolean; messageId: string; reply: { conversationRef: string; messageId: string; text: string; timestamp: number; replyToId?: string; threadId?: string; transcriptArtifactId?: string; transcriptMessageId?: string }; status: "replied" } | { channel: string; conversationRef: string; correlationPersisted: boolean; messageId: string; status: "timeout" } | { channel: string; conversationRef: string; correlationPersisted: boolean; error: string; status: "sent" | "queued" | "suppressed" | "unknown"; messageId?: string }
- edit { edits: Array<{ newText: string; oldText: string }>; path: string } -> { changed: false } | { changed: true; diff: string; patch: string; firstChangedLine?: number }
- portal { action: "open" | "list" | "close"; description?: string; environmentId?: string; id?: string; path?: string; port?: number /* integer, >= 1, <= 65535 */; title?: string } -> { createdAtMs: number; id: string; listenPort: number; port: number; publicUrl: string; title: string; description?: string; origin?: string; path?: string; tokenQuery?: string; url?: string } | { portals: Array<{ createdAtMs: number; id: string; listenPort: number; port: number; publicUrl: string; title: string; description?: string; origin?: string; path?: string; tokenQuery?: string; url?: string }> } | { closed: boolean }
- read { path: string; cursor?: number /* integer, >= 0 */; limit?: number; offset?: number /* integer, >= 1 */; optional?: true } -> { content: string; kind: "text" } | { content: string; kind: "image"; mimeType: string } | { content: string; continuation: { kind: "line"; offset: number; limit?: number } | { cursor: number; kind: "cursor"; offset: number; limit?: number }; kind: "truncated"; truncation: { firstLineExceedsLimit: boolean; lastLinePartial: boolean; maxBytes: number; maxLines: number; outputBytes: number; outputLines: number; totalBytes: number; totalLines: number; truncated: true; truncatedBy: "lines" | "bytes" } } | { kind: "not_found"; optional: true; path: string; status: "not_found" }
